; What the Orchestrate Nexus remembers: one Memory store, holding the
; standard Nexus metadata tree, where the Nexus was last bound, a declared
; move not yet completed, the Locks it holds, and the LockId the next Lock
; takes. A held Lock is the contract's own Lock, stored whole. The
; metadata tree holds the Nexus's Configuration: the desired configuration
; and whether the meta Configure has been done.
;
; Two families are read only from an older store. StoredConfiguration is
; the desired configuration as 0.30 and 0.31 kept it, before the metadata
; tree; it seeds the tree once and is cleared. StoredPathLock is the
; pre-0.25 PathLock; a store still holding one is refused, never imported.
;
; Every record archives to the bytes the hand-written record it replaces
; wrote, so a store written before this file opens unchanged.
Memory
[ signal_orchestrate:[ Lock LockId OrchestrateNexusConfiguration ]
  nexus:[ ConfigurationState Situation Relocation ] ]
[ StoredMetadata.{ Configuration.ConfigurationState<OrchestrateNexusConfiguration> }
  StoredSituation.{ Situation }
  StoredRelocation.{ Relocation }
  StoredLock.{ Lock }
  StoredAllocator.{ LockId }
  StoredConfiguration.{ OrchestrateNexusConfiguration }
  PathLockName.String
  PathLockPath.String
  PathLockPaths.Vector<PathLockPath>
  PathLockDescription.String
  PathLock.{ PathLockName PathLockPaths PathLockDescription }
  StoredPathLock.{ PathLockName PathLock } ]
